{% doc %}
  @prompt
    That is a very valid point. Using Shopify Navigation menus (link_list) makes linking directly to uploaded PDFs clunky, as you have to grab the file URL first and build the menu separately.
    
    By switching the logic to use Shopify Blocks, you will be able to click an "Add Link" button directly inside the Theme Editor for that section, which natively allows you to select files (like your PDFs) right from your Shopify library.
    
    Because standard blocks just dump everything into one list, the trick here is to ask the AI to create different block types so you can assign a link specifically to Box 1, Box 2, or Box 3.
    
    Here is the revised prompt to generate that exact setup:
    
    The Revised Prompt
    Create a custom Shopify Liquid section for a "Knowledge Base & Resource Portal". The design should feature a clean, professional 2x2 grid on desktop that stacks to a single column on mobile.
    
    Instead of using Navigation menus, this section must use Blocks so I can easily add links and attach PDF files directly from the theme editor.
    
    Here are the specific requirements for the layout and schema:
    
    1. Section Settings:
    
    Section Title (Text)
    
    Section Subtitle (Rich text)
    
    Card 1: Description (Rich Text), Button Text, Button Link
    
    Card 2: Description (Rich Text)
    
    Card 3: Description (Rich Text)
    
    Card 4: Description (Rich Text), Button Text, Button Link
    
    2. Block Requirements:
    Create three distinct block types so I can assign links to specific cards. Every block type should have two settings: "Link Label" (Text) and "File/Page URL" (URL picker).
    
    Block Type 1: machine_link (Name: "Machine Spec Link")
    
    Block Type 2: cut_sheet_link (Name: "Cut Sheet Link")
    
    Block Type 3: brochure_link (Name: "Brochure/How-To Link")
    
    3. Grid & Styling Requirements:
    
    Four distinct card containers (2 columns x 2 rows on desktop).
    
    Cards should have a subtle border, rounded corners, and a light background (clean corporate UI).
    
    Cards 1, 2, and 3 must feature a custom CSS scrollable container (max-height: 300px; overflow-y: auto;) for their link lists. This is critical so the cards remain a uniform size even when loaded with dozens of block links.
    
    Include a static SVG icon at the top of each card.
    
    4. Liquid Logic for Cards:
    
    Card 1 (Machine Specifications): Output the section settings for the description. Then, create a for loop that iterates through section.blocks. Use an if statement to only output blocks where block.type == 'machine_link' inside the scrollable container. Output the Contact Us button below the scrollable list.
    
    Card 2 (Cut Data Sheets): Output the description setting. Loop through section.blocks and only output blocks where block.type == 'cut_sheet_link' inside the scrollable container.
    
    Card 3 (Brochures): Output the description setting. Loop through section.blocks and only output blocks where block.type == 'brochure_link' inside the scrollable container.
    
    Card 4 (Safety Data Sheets): Output the description setting and the prominent SDS Button setting (no block loop needed here).
    
    Please provide the complete, ready-to-use Liquid code. Include the {% schema %}, the HTML structure, and the necessary CSS within a <style> tag to ensure the grid responsiveness and the scrollable link containers work perfectly., Also please add a width tool that allows me to fix the maximum width on this section
{% enddoc %}

{% assign ai_gen_id = block.id | replace: '_', '' | downcase %}

{% style %}
  .ai-knowledge-base-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    padding: 60px 20px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-container-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-width: {{ block.settings.max_width }}px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-header-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-title-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: 36px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #0e1b4d;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-subtitle-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #0e1b4d;
    opacity: 0.8;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 28px;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-card-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid rgba(14, 27, 77, 0.1);
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: 32px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(14, 27, 77, 0.05);
    transition: box-shadow 0.3s ease;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-card-{{ ai_gen_id }}:hover {
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(14, 27, 77, 0.1);
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-card-icon-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    color: #4770db;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-card-icon-{{ ai_gen_id }} svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-card-description-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #0e1b4d;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-card-description-{{ ai_gen_id }} p {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-card-description-{{ ai_gen_id }} p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-scrollable-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-height: 300px;
    overflow-y: auto;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    padding-right: 8px;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-scrollable-{{ ai_gen_id }}::-webkit-scrollbar {
    width: 6px;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-scrollable-{{ ai_gen_id }}::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
    background: rgba(14, 27, 77, 0.05);
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-scrollable-{{ ai_gen_id }}::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
    background: rgba(71, 112, 219, 0.3);
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-scrollable-{{ ai_gen_id }}::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {
    background: rgba(71, 112, 219, 0.5);
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-link-list-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-link-item-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-link-item-{{ ai_gen_id }}:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-link-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    color: #4770db;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 14px;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-link-{{ ai_gen_id }}:hover {
    color: #0e1b4d;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-link-{{ ai_gen_id }}::before {
    content: '→';
    font-size: 16px;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-link-{{ ai_gen_id }}:hover::before {
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-button-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 14px 28px;
    background-color: #0e1b4d;
    color: #ffffff;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 40px;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: background-color 0.3s ease;
    border: 1px solid #0e1b4d;
    align-self: flex-start;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-button-{{ ai_gen_id }}:hover {
    background-color: #4770db;
    border-color: #4770db;
  }

  .ai-knowledge-base-empty-state-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    padding: 20px;
    text-align: center;
    color: rgba(14, 27, 77, 0.5);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-style: italic;
    background: rgba(14, 27, 77, 0.02);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .ai-knowledge-base-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      padding: 40px 16px;
    }

    .ai-knowledge-base-title-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: 28px;
    }

    .ai-knowledge-base-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 20px;
    }

    .ai-knowledge-base-card-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      padding: 24px;
    }

    .ai-knowledge-base-scrollable-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      max-height: 250px;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

